This directory contains:
README            --- this file
fix_atomtype.pl   --- perl script for fixing atom types in BOSS Z-matrix
viagra.azmat_log  --- see below
viagra.boss
viagra.mol2
viagra.sum
viagra_new.boss
viagra_new.mol2

----------------
Purpose: This series of conversions will take a MOL2 file, convert it
         to BOSS Z-matrix, perform a QM calc (AM1 or PM3) which gives
         CM1 or Mullien charges and generates new OPLS atom types.
         Then the BOSS Z-matrix is converted back to MOL2 format with
         updated QM charges.
         Atom numberings are changed when converting to BOSS from MOL2,
         since Z-matrix must be created in an intelligent way.
         Changed numberings are printed out if '-V' option is specified.
         I think you can rearrange the atoms in the final MOL2 file,
         in order to match the original atom numberings.

         -DC, May 20, 1999
         lim@doctor.chem.yale.edu

1. Create a BOSS Z-matrix for QM calculation.

% autozmat -i mol2 -o qm_boss -V -f viagra.boss viagra.mol2 >& viagra.azmat_log

  <NOTE>
    -i mol2	--- input format = MOL2
    -o qm_boss  --- output format = BOSS Z-matrix for QM calc
    -V          --- verbose
    -f viagra.boss  --- save the output in viagra.boss
    viagra.mol2     --- input file name
    >& viagra.azmat_log  --- save the error messages in viagra.azmat_log
                             (in thise case, this file will include
                              changes in atom numbering)

2. Now you have a BOSS z-matrix which can be submitted to QM calc.
   Run BOSS.

3. Upon the completion of BOSS job, you'll have a new BOSS z-matrix
   in the summary file where new OPLS atom types (starting from 800)
   are attached to the end of a normal BOSS Z-matrix.

   There is one problem, i.e., in the Z-matrix, atom types are merely
   atomic numbers as in

   1  X    -1    0    0    0.000000   0    0.000000   0    0.000000        0
   2  X    -1    0    1    1.000000   0    0.000000   0    0.000000        0
   3  C     6    0    2    1.000000   1   90.000000   0    0.000000        0
   4  N     7    0    3    1.406890   2  151.424170   1  180.000000        0
   ...

   We need to change this so that it appears as below.
   1  X    -1    0    0    0.000000   0    0.000000   0    0.000000        0
   2  X    -1    0    1    1.000000   0    0.000000   0    0.000000        0
   3  C   800    0    2    1.000000   1   90.000000   0    0.000000        0
   4  N   801    0    3    1.406890   2  151.424170   1  180.000000        0
   ...

   You may do it by hand, but you can use a PERL scrip shown below
   to save time. Save it as 'fix_atomtype.pl' or whatever and make it
   executable (chmod +x fix_atomtype.pl). If perl is installed in
   other than /usr/local/bin/perl, change the first line appropriately.

#------- CUT HERE -------
#!/usr/local/bin/perl

$nlines = 0;
$current_type = 800;

MAIN: {
        while (<>) {
                $nlines++;
                $type = substr($_, 9, 4);
                if ($nlines == 1 || $type == -1) {print; next;}
                if ($type =~ /^[ ]*$/ || !($type =~ /^[ ]*[0-9]+[ ]*$/)) {print; last;}
                printf("%s%4d%s", substr($_,0,9), $current_type, substr($_,13,9999));
                $current_type++;
        }
        while (<>) {print;}
}
#------- CUT HERE -------

4. Using this perl script (fix_atomtype.pl), fix atom types int the Z-matrix.

% fix_atomtype.pl viagra.sum > viagra_new.boss

5. Convert the BOSS Z-matrix back to MOL2 format.

% autozmat -i boss -o mol2 -f viagra_new.mol2 viagra_new.boss

  <NOTE>
    -i boss   --- input format = BOSS Z-matrix
                  Do not use '-i qm_boss' because this will cause autozmat to
                  interprete atom types as atomic nubmers. We want to use
                  atom types attached to the Z-matrix.
    -o boss   --- output format = MOL2
    -f viagra_new.mol2 --- save the output in viagra_new.mol2
    viagra_new.zmat    --- input file

